---
description: Used when implementing or refactoring code
alwaysApply: false
---

- Write short and concise code.
- Use meaningful variable and function names.
- Function names should explain what they do, needing no additional comments.
- Use comments sparingly, only when it is impossible to explain why the code is written the way it is.
- Use type hints for all functions and variables, the project should be strongly typed.
- Use StrEnums for string literals, the code should have no hardcoded strings, though exceptions may apply.
- All code must be written with testability in mind, unit tests should be able to be written without mocking or patching.
- Use PEP-8 style for all Python code.
- Avoid using emojis in code.